{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":408,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Then Bildad the Shuhite answered,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1289},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":409,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“How long will you hunt for words? Consider, and afterwards we will speak.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1291},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":410,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"Why are we counted as animals, which have become unclean in your sight?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1294},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":411,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"You who tear yourself in your anger, will the earth be forsaken for you? Or will the rock be removed out of its place?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1297},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":412,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"“Yes, the light of the wicked will be put out. The spark of his fire won’t shine.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1302},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":413,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"The light will be dark in his tent. His lamp above him will be put out.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1305},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":414,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"The steps of his strength will be shortened. His own counsel will cast him down.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1308},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":415,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"For he is cast into a net by his own feet, and he wanders into its mesh.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1311},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":416,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"A snare will take him by the heel. A trap will catch him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1314},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":417,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"A noose is hidden for him in the ground, a trap for him on the path.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1317},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":418,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"Terrors will make him afraid on every side, and will chase him at his heels.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1320},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":419,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"His strength will be famished. Calamity will be ready at his side.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1323},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":420,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"The members of his body will be devoured. The firstborn of death will devour his members.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1326},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":421,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"He will be rooted out of the security of his tent. He will be brought to the king of terrors.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1329},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":422,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"There will dwell in his tent that which is none of his. Sulfur will be scattered on his habitation.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1332},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":423,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"His roots will be dried up beneath. His branch will be cut off above.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1335},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":424,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"His memory will perish from the earth. He will have no name in the street.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1338},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":425,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"He will be driven from light into darkness, and chased out of the world.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1341},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":426,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"He will have neither son nor grandson among his people, nor any remaining where he lived.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1344},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":427,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"Those who come after will be astonished at his day, as those who went before were frightened.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1347},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":18,"verse_ordinal":428,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"Surely such are the dwellings of the unrighteous. This is the place of him who doesn’t know God.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1350}]}